====Major appearances====
=====[[Ash's Chimchar|Paul's/Ash's Chimchar]]=====
When [[Paul]] first appeared, he commanded a Chimchar in ''[[DP003|When Pokémon Worlds Collide!]]''. In ''[[DP051|Glory Blaze]]'', Paul {{pkmn2|released}} him before {{Ash}} {{pkmn2|caught}} him in ''[[DP052|Smells Like Team Spirit]]''. He evolved into a Monferno in ''[[DP132|Evolving Strategies!]]'' and later into an Infernape in ''[[DP163|Fighting Ire with Fire!]]''.

=====[[Flint's Chimchar]]=====
[[Flint]] received his Infernape as a Chimchar, as seen in ''[[DP165|Flint Sparks the Fire!]]''. It evolved all the way to Infernape prior to the events of the episode.

=====[[Team Poképals]]=====
Chimchar was one of the two main members of Team Poképals, which appeared in ''[[Pokémon Mystery Dungeon: Explorers of Time & Darkness]]'' and ''[[Pokémon Mystery Dungeon: Explorers of Sky - Beyond Time & Darkness]]''.

=====Other=====
[[File:Goh Sobble Egg.png|thumb|250px|A Chimchar Egg (right) in {{aniseries|JN}}]]
Chimchar debuted in ''[[DP001|Following A Maiden's Voyage!]]'', where it was teasing a {{TP|Dawn|Piplup}} after stealing {{pkmn|food}} from it. Piplup then started firing a {{m|Bubble Beam}} attack, but Chimchar kept jumping out of the way. {{p|Staraptor}} was hit in Piplup's line of fire and created a {{m|Whirlwind}} that wrecked everything in [[Professor Rowan]]'s lab. Chimchar jumped out of a broken window, with Piplup chasing after it.

In ''[[M10|The Rise of Darkrai]]'', [[Alice]] uses a Chimchar to power her hot air balloon with {{m|Flamethrower}}. It reappeared in the ending credits of ''[[M12|Arceus and the Jewel of Life]]''.

In [[DPS01]], [[Professor Rowan]] presented a Chimchar to [[Shinko]] as one of the first partner Pokémon for her to pick. A situation similar to ''Following A Maiden's Voyage!'' occurred, with Chimchar and {{p|Piplup}} starting a fight, leading to a window breaking and Chimchar and Piplup escaping. They were then captured by an {{p|Ariados}}'s web before being rescued by Shinko and {{an|Dawn}}.

In ''[[PK27|Pikachu and the Pokémon Music Squad]]'', a Chimchar was living in a forest.

In ''[[JN090|Showdown at the Gates of Warp!]]'', [[Alternate World Ash]]'s Infernape [[Devolution|devolved]] into Monferno, then Chimchar, and finally an {{pkmn|Egg}} due to {{OBP|Dialga|recurring}} and {{OBP|Palkia|recurring}}'s influence. It was later restored to normal.

====Minor appearances====
In ''[[DP004|Dawn of a New Era!]]'', a {{pkmn|Trainer}}'s Chimchar was at a [[Pokémon Center]].

A Chimchar appeared in ''[[DP071|Pokémon Ranger and the Kidnapped Riolu! (Part 1)]]''.

In ''[[DP126|Classroom Training!]]'', a young boy used a Chimchar to battle a {{p|Turtwig}} at the {{ci|Snowpoint}} {{pkmn|Trainers' School}}. A flashback featured another Chimchar under the command of a young [[Zoey]].

In ''[[PK24|Meloetta's Moonlight Serenade]]'', a Chimchar watched {{an|Meloetta}}'s concert.

In ''[[SM034|A Crowning Moment of Truth!]]'', two Trainers' Chimchar attended the [[Wela Fire Festival]].

A Chimchar appeared in a fantasy alongside the other [[first partner Pokémon]] in ''[[JN046|Getting More Than You Battled For!]]''.

A Chimchar appeared in ''[[HZ001|The Pendant That Starts It All (Part One)]]'', under the ownership of a student of [[Indigo Academy]].

